# VeridianOS system call numbers (ADR 0009).
#
# The single source of the user ABI: every kernel `Syscall` variant, the
# Linux x86_64 system call it implements (its number comes from
# abi/linux/syscall_64.tbl), or `private N` for a VeridianOS call with no
# Linux equivalent. Private numbers are 1024 + the call's pre-v0.27 native
# number, far above Linux's range (471 in v7.2), and never change.
#
# tools/compat/gen_syscalls.py turns this file into
#   kernel/src/syscall/numbers.rs              (the enum and its decoder)
#   userland/libc/include/veridian/sysno.h     (SYS_* for the native libc)
#   userland/abi/syscall_numbers.rs            (SYS_* for rust-std and vsh)
# and `gen_syscalls.py --check` fails CI when any of them is stale.
#
# Format: one call per line, either
#   <linux name>                 a Linux call: the kernel variant is the name
#                                in CamelCase (rt_sigaction -> RtSigaction),
#                                the C and Rust constant SYS_<linux name>
#   <Variant> private <number>   a VeridianOS call: the constant is
#                                SYS_<VARIANT_IN_UPPER_SNAKE_CASE>
# Each call has exactly one name in each language.
# A `## Heading` line starts a group (a comment in the generated enum).

